            "text": "An efficient implementation in Python to compute the sum of Euclidean distances over all ordered pairs of rows.\n\n### Method Explanation\n\nThe input array contains 8,000 vectors in 1,024 dimensions. Computing all $8000 \\times 8000 = 64,000,000$ pairwise Euclidean distances using explicit differences or Python loops causes severe memory allocation overhead and single-threaded execution bottlenecks that lead to timeouts.\n\nWe can compute the exact pairwise squared Euclidean distances efficiently using matrix multiplication:\n$$\\|x_i - x_j\\|_2^2 = \\|x_i\\|_2^2 + \\|x_j\\|_2^2 - 2 (x_i \\cdot x_j)$$\n\n1. Subtracting the mean vector beforehand ensures translation invariance ($\\|x_i - x_j\\| = \\|(x_i - c) - (x_j - c)\\|$) and centers the data, guarding against catastrophic cancellation.\n2. Casting to `float64` maintains high numerical precision throughout.\n3. The Gram matrix $G = X X^T$ leverages multi-threaded BLAS GEMM kernels, running in seconds.\n4. Performing operations in-place on the distance matrix keeps peak memory usage around 512 MB and maximizes cache efficiency.\n\n### Python Source Code\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Load input array\n    vectors = np.load('vectors.npy')\n    \n    # Convert to float64 for numerical precision\n    X = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n    \n    # Center vectors to maximize numerical stability (Euclidean distance is translation-invariant)\n    X -= np.mean(X, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    \n    # Squared norms of each row\n    sq = np.sum(X ** 2, axis=1)\n    \n    # Compute Gram matrix using optimized multi-threaded BLAS\n    G = X @ X.T\n    \n    # Compute squared Euclidean distances in-place: sq_i + sq_j - 2 * (x_i . x_j)\n    G *= -2.0\n    G += sq[:, None]\n    G += sq[None, :]\n    \n    # Ensure exact zero on the diagonal and clip any numerical underflow below zero\n    np.fill_diagonal(G, 0.0)\n    np.maximum(G, 0.0, out=G)\n    np.sqrt(G, out=G)\n    \n    total = float(np.sum(G))\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
